# The ticket spec (orchestration's DESIGN §4). Every ticket overwrites it
# wholly, so two tickets whose lifetimes overlap conflict on it every time
# and over the whole file — and the resolution is always ours, because the
# other ticket's spec is already in history on its own merge.
#
# Resolved by git rather than by the agent on purpose: left to a pass, it
# is a conflict that is always safe to take blindly, and learning to take
# it blindly is the habit you do not want in the same merge where a real
# collision in a systems doc has to be read carefully.
#
# The driver is defined in the agent job (`git config merge.ours.driver
# true`), because git does not ship one. Without that config git falls
# back to an ordinary conflict, which is loud rather than wrong.
CHANGE.md merge=ours
